# What must not reach the build context.
#
# `.env*` is first because it is the one with consequences: `turbo.json`
# declares those files a `build` input, and a development database URL copied
# into an image is a production secret's worth of surprise waiting in a layer.
# Real credentials reach the app through `fly secrets` (NFR24, runbook §1).
#
# **Both forms, and the recursive one is the one that matters.** Docker matches
# these against the whole context-relative path, so a bare `.env` excludes
# `./.env` and nothing else — while the only `.env.local` this repo ever has is
# at `apps/web/.env.local`, because that is the directory `next dev` reads it
# from. Written root-anchored, this block excluded nothing that exists, and
# `fly deploy` builds on a **remote** builder, so a developer's `RESEND_API_KEY`
# would have been uploaded off their machine into a builder layer cache. Every
# other pattern here already carries its `**/` twin; this one did not.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
.git
.github
coverage
**/coverage

# Agent surfaces and generated review artifacts. None of it is built, and
# `.agents/` alone is tens of megabytes of vendored skills.
.claude
.agents
.impeccable
.codex

# The go-live wizard's gitignored transcript, which is one operator's run.
.go-live-facts
.go-live-evidence.md
